# live-only.manifest — every REAL file that legitimately exists in a live executed surface
# (~/.claude/{bin,hooks,hooks/lib,scripts,scripts/lib,scripts/limit-recover,lib}) while having NO
# counterpart content anywhere in this checkout's tracked tree.
#
# Read by scripts/deploy-link-parity.sh's STRAY leg. A live real file that matches no row and whose
# bytes are in no tracked file is reported STRAY — the "untracked hand-placed tool" defect: bin/cc-mail
# sat live and unversioned for 5 days (and bin/cc-thread before it, both hand-placed by peer sessions
# working in other repos) while link-parity, which only ever walked checkout→live, read "0 actionable".
#
# WHY A MANIFEST AND NOT A BARE live→checkout DIFF. The naive check convicts the copy-deploy state:
# ~/.claude/bin/it2 is a real file BY DESIGN, cp'd from the tracked bin/it2-wrapper under a DIFFERENT
# NAME (install.sh:593, scripts/kitty-setup.sh:215). That shape needs no row — the leg matches by
# CONTENT, not by path, so a renamed copy is recognised automatically and name-independently. Rows are
# needed only for the residue that content-matching CANNOT see: a file the checkout never contains.
# Getting this backwards is the sibling-auditors-disagree failure this repo has already paid for
# (memory sibling-auditors-must-share-the-state-model — one check modelled "unlinked BY DESIGN" and
# its sibling convicted the live layer for obeying the design).
#
# THE WITNESS COLUMN IS THE ANTI-ROT DEVICE. A row is not a permanent licence: it names a tracked file
# that must still exist AND still mention the artifact. Delete or rename that producer and the row goes
# STALE, which is reported as a FINDING — never as a silent exemption. An exemption whose reason has
# dissolved is exactly how a stale premise keeps laundering a real defect (memory
# discovery-critic-premise-goes-stale: re-check the premise at CONSUMPTION, and fail toward reporting).
#
# NOT COVERED, DELIBERATELY — and measured, not assumed (2026-08-08):
#   · SYMLINKS of every kind. A live link into this checkout is the forward walk's business; a link
#     pointing ANYWHERE ELSE is explicitly not ours to judge (tests/deploy-link-parity.bats:156 — "a
#     dangling one there is that repo's business, and flagging it would train the operator to ignore
#     this report"). ~/.claude/bin carries 5 such links into claude-session-search today. The cost of
#     honouring that contract is that a hand-placed link to a non-repo path is missed; the defect that
#     actually recurred twice was a hand-placed real FILE, which is what this leg catches.
#   · PROMPT-DOCUMENT surfaces — skills/, agents/, commands/. Live-only content there is the NORMAL
#     path, not a defect. The exclusion stands; both of its numbers were re-measured 2026-08-18 and
#     the FIRST one was misleading in the direction that matters:
#       — SKILL DIRECTORIES: 5 of 35 now, not 20. f542c8b2c tracked 13 and 8b33db9e6/ab62d3a08 two
#         more; the surviving 5 are third-party derivatives, each with a durable reason recorded in
#         skills/LOCAL_ONLY.md (motion + the two Vercel guides are vendored upstream text;
#         pyramid-principle-full is a derivative of a copyrighted book, deliberately never committed;
#         pyramid-principle's SKILL.md is a symlink into another tracked repo).
#       — WHAT THIS LEG WOULD ACTUALLY PRINT: 82 lines, not 5, and not 20. The STRAY leg reports
#         FILES; those 5 directories hold 84 files (82 real, 2 symlinks it already excludes) —
#         react-best-practices alone is 59. Reading "20 of the 35 live skills" as the size of the
#         wall conflates a DIRECTORY count with a FILE count and understates it 4x. So the
#         alarm-polarity case for excluding skills/ is STRONGER than when it was written, not
#         weaker — do not "re-open this now that it is only 5".
#     Widening this leg to skills/ therefore requires the 5 declarations FIRST — glob rows
#     (`skills/<name>/*`, the form lib/*.prelink-bak already uses) witnessed by skills/LOCAL_ONLY.md —
#     and is only worth it as one unit, because the rows are inert until the sweep reaches them.
#     agents/motion-reviewer.md is a real file in no checkout and is the same class.
#     The defect class this leg exists for is an EXECUTABLE silently entering PATH, not a document.
#     The unversioned-skills gap is real and separately filed (backlog bb2495b098b8).
#   · DIRECTORIES. hooks/lib and scripts/lib are structural; the three live __pycache__ dirs are
#     bytecode residue of the *.py hooks. Neither is a hand-placed tool.
#
# FORMAT — 4 TAB-separated columns, '#' comments and blank lines ignored:
#   <live-relative-path>  <kind>  <witness>  <why>
#     live-relative-path : path under ~/.claude. A leading '*' in the BASENAME is a wildcard
#                          (lib/*.prelink-bak). The literal remainder is also what the witness must
#                          mention, so a row cannot drift away from its own producer silently.
#     kind               : build   — compiled from a tracked source; the repo carries no binaries
#                          residue — written on purpose by a tracked script, and kept
#     witness            : repo-relative path that must EXIST and must CONTAIN the match stem
#     why                : one line, for the human reading a report

bin/kitty-pane-menu-native	build	scripts/kitty-setup.sh	swiftc -O of the tracked bin/kitty-pane-menu-native.swift; a compiled binary cannot be symlinked and the repo does not carry binaries (kitty-setup.sh:239-246)
lib/*.prelink-bak	residue	docs/activation/pending-activation/15-shared-task-board-activate.sh	the activation script deliberately preserves the previous REAL file before replacing it with a link, so the operator can recover it (15-shared-task-board-activate.sh:67)
